      "pali": "Saṁyutta Nikāya 35.157 ",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 35.157 "
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "16. Nandikkhayavagga ",
      "english": "16. The End of Relishing "
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "Bāhiranandikkhayasutta ",
      "english": "The Exterior and the End of Relishing "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "“Anicceyeva, bhikkhave, bhikkhu rūpe aniccāti passati, sāssa hoti sammādiṭṭhi. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, sights really are impermanent. A mendicant sees that they are impermanent: that’s their right view. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "Sammā passaṁ nibbindati. ",
      "english": "Seeing rightly, they grow disillusioned. "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "Nandikkhayā rāgakkhayo; ",
      "english": "When relishing ends, greed ends. When greed ends, relishing ends. "
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "rāgakkhayā nandikkhayo. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "Nandirāgakkhayā cittaṁ suvimuttanti vuccati. ",
      "english": "When relishing and greed end, the mind is said to be well freed. "
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "Anicceyeva, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sadde … ",
      "english": "Sounds … "
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "gandhe … ",
      "english": "Smells … "
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "rase … ",
      "english": "Tastes … "
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "phoṭṭhabbe … ",
      "english": "Touches … "
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "dhamme aniccāti passati, sāssa hoti sammādiṭṭhi. ",
      "english": "Ideas really are impermanent. A mendicant sees that they are impermanent: that’s their right view. "
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "Sammā passaṁ nibbindati. ",
      "english": "Seeing rightly, they grow disillusioned. "
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "Nandikkhayā rāgakkhayo; ",
      "english": "When relishing ends, greed ends. When greed ends, relishing ends. "
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "rāgakkhayā nandikkhayo. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "Nandirāgakkhayā cittaṁ suvimuttanti vuccatī”ti. ",
      "english": "When relishing and greed end, the mind is said to be well freed.” "
